E('mark twain|huckleberry finn|tom sawyer', 'Mark Twain was an American writer and humorist.', 'He lived from 1835 to 1910; his real name was Samuel Clemens.', 'He wrote The Adventures of Tom Sawyer and Adventures of Huckleberry Finn.', 'He worked as a Mississippi riverboat pilot; “mark twain” was a river depth call.', 'He was famous for wit, like “the reports of my death are greatly exaggerated”.', 'Hemingway said all modern American literature comes from Huckleberry Finn.')
E('ernest hemingway|hemingway', 'Ernest Hemingway was an American novelist.', 'He lived from 1899 to 1961.', 'His books include The Old Man and the Sea and A Farewell to Arms.', 'He wrote in short, simple sentences.', 'He was an ambulance driver in the First World War.', 'He won the Nobel Prize in Literature in 1954.')
E('virginia woolf', 'Virginia Woolf was an English modernist writer.', 'She lived from 1882 to 1941.', 'Her novels include Mrs Dalloway and To the Lighthouse.', 'Her essay A Room of One’s Own argued women need money and space to write.', 'She was part of the Bloomsbury Group.')
E('edgar allan poe|poe|the raven', 'Edgar Allan Poe was an American writer of mystery and horror.', 'He lived from 1809 to 1849.', 'His poem The Raven made him famous.', 'He is credited with inventing the detective story.', 'His tales include The Tell-Tale Heart.', 'His death remains a mystery.')
E('arthur conan doyle|sherlock holmes|conan doyle', 'Sir Arthur Conan Doyle was a Scottish writer who created Sherlock Holmes.', 'He lived from 1859 to 1930; Holmes first appeared in 1887.', 'He was a doctor.', 'Holmes lived at 221B Baker Street with Dr Watson.', 'Doyle killed Holmes off in 1893 but brought him back due to public demand.', 'Holmes never actually says “Elementary, my dear Watson” in the books.')
E('agatha christie|christie', 'Agatha Christie was an English crime novelist.', 'She lived from 1890 to 1976.', 'She created the detectives Hercule Poirot and Miss Marple.', 'She is the best-selling novelist of all time.', 'Her play The Mousetrap has run in London since 1952.', 'She once disappeared for 11 days in 1926.')
E('j k rowling|harry potter|rowling', 'J. K. Rowling is a British author best known for the Harry Potter series.', 'The first book was published in 1997.', 'She wrote it partly in Edinburgh cafés.', 'It was rejected by several publishers.', 'The seven books have sold over 500 million copies.', 'They were adapted into eight films.')
E('victor hugo|les miserables|les misérables', 'Victor Hugo was a French writer.', 'He lived from 1802 to 1885.', 'He wrote Les Misérables and The Hunchback of Notre-Dame.', 'He was a passionate campaigner against the death penalty.', 'He lived in exile for nearly 20 years.', 'His funeral drew around two million people.')
E('emily dickinson', 'Emily Dickinson was an American poet.', 'She lived from 1830 to 1886.', 'She wrote nearly 1,800 poems.', 'Fewer than a dozen were published in her lifetime.', 'She lived mostly in seclusion in Massachusetts.', 'Her unusual punctuation and short lines made her a pioneer.')
E('maya angelou', 'Maya Angelou was an American poet, memoirist and activist.', 'She lived from 1928 to 2014.', 'Her memoir I Know Why the Caged Bird Sings appeared in 1969.', 'She worked with Martin Luther King Jr. and Malcolm X.', 'She read a poem at Bill Clinton’s inauguration in 1993.')
E('chopin|frederic chopin', 'Frédéric Chopin was a Polish composer and pianist.', 'He lived from 1810 to 1849.', 'He wrote mainly for the piano.', 'His works include nocturnes, waltzes and mazurkas.', 'He lived in Paris from 1831.', 'His heart was buried in Warsaw.')
E('tchaikovsky', 'Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky was a Russian composer.', 'He lived from 1840 to 1893.', 'He wrote the ballets Swan Lake, The Sleeping Beauty and The Nutcracker.', 'His 1812 Overture includes real cannon fire.', 'He is one of the most popular composers.')
E('vivaldi|four seasons', 'Antonio Vivaldi was an Italian Baroque composer.', 'He lived from 1678 to 1741.', 'He wrote The Four Seasons, a set of violin concertos.', 'He was a priest, nicknamed “the Red Priest” for his hair.', 'He taught music at an orphanage for girls in Venice.')
E('louis armstrong|jazz', 'Louis Armstrong was an American jazz trumpeter and singer.', 'He lived from 1901 to 1971.', 'He grew up poor in New Orleans, the birthplace of jazz.', 'He helped make jazz a soloist’s art.', 'His hits include What a Wonderful World.', 'He was nicknamed “Satchmo”.')
E('bob marley|reggae', 'Bob Marley was a Jamaican reggae musician.', 'He lived from 1945 to 1981.', 'He made reggae famous worldwide.', 'His songs include No Woman, No Cry and One Love.', 'He was a follower of Rastafari.', 'He was shot in 1976 but played a concert two days later.')
E('queen band|freddie mercury|bohemian rhapsody', 'Queen was a British rock band fronted by Freddie Mercury.', 'They formed in 1970.', 'Their hits include Bohemian Rhapsody and We Will Rock You.', 'Their Live Aid performance in 1985 is legendary.', 'Freddie Mercury died in 1991.')
E('hollywood|charlie chaplin|chaplin', 'Hollywood is the centre of the American film industry, and Charlie Chaplin was one of its first great stars.', 'Chaplin lived from 1889 to 1977.', 'He created the character of the Tramp.', 'His films include The Kid and Modern Times.', 'He mocked Hitler in The Great Dictator in 1940.', 'Hollywood grew in the 1910s thanks to sunny weather and cheap land.')
E('walt disney|disney|mickey mouse', 'Walt Disney was an American animator and entrepreneur.', 'He lived from 1901 to 1966.', 'He co-created Mickey Mouse, who debuted in Steamboat Willie in 1928.', 'Snow White (1937) was the first full-length cel-animated feature film.', 'He opened Disneyland in 1955.', 'He won a record 22 Academy Awards.')
E('marilyn monroe', 'Marilyn Monroe was an American actress and icon.', 'She lived from 1926 to 1962.', 'She was born Norma Jeane Mortenson.', 'Her films include Some Like It Hot.', 'She sang “Happy Birthday” to President Kennedy in 1962.', 'She died at 36.')
E('andy warhol|pop art', 'Andy Warhol was an American artist and leader of Pop Art.', 'He lived from 1928 to 1987.', 'He made famous prints of Campbell’s soup cans and Marilyn Monroe.', 'He predicted everyone would be “world-famous for 15 minutes”.', 'His studio was called The Factory.')
E('salvador dali|dali|surrealism', 'Salvador Dalí was a Spanish Surrealist painter.', 'He lived from 1904 to 1989.', 'His painting The Persistence of Memory shows melting clocks.', 'Surrealism explored dreams and the unconscious.', 'He was famous for his upturned moustache.')
E('botticelli|birth of venus', 'Sandro Botticelli was an Italian Renaissance painter.', 'He lived from about 1445 to 1510.', 'He painted The Birth of Venus and Primavera.', 'He worked for the Medici.', 'His work fell out of fashion until the 19th century.')
E('raphael', 'Raphael was an Italian painter and architect of the High Renaissance.', 'He lived from 1483 to 1520.', 'He painted The School of Athens in the Vatican.', 'It shows Plato, Aristotle and other philosophers.', 'He died at 37.', 'He is one of the trio of great High Renaissance masters with Leonardo and Michelangelo.')
E('banksy', 'Banksy is an anonymous street artist from England.', 'His work became famous from the 1990s.', 'He uses stencils to paint satirical images on walls.', 'His identity has never been officially confirmed.', 'In 2018 one of his paintings shredded itself just after it sold at auction.')
